WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.818
Three workers settle payments from one Redis stream.

2
00:00:05.818 --> 00:00:09.775
If a worker dies holding three payments, how does anyone find out?

3
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:13.042
A stream is a log in one key, kept in memory.

4
00:00:13.042 --> 00:00:19.601
XADD appends an entry, and Redis gives it an ID made of its clock in milliseconds and a counter.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.933
A consumer group splits the stream among workers.

6
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:29.008
w1 asks for entries never delivered to anyone in the group, and Redis hands it the first three.

7
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:38.529
Redis writes each delivery into the group's pending entries list: the entry, its owner, how long it's been idle, and how many times it was delivered.

8
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.875
w2 gets the other two, settles them, and acknowledges them with XACK, which removes them from the list.

9
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.979
w1 is killed before it acknowledges anything.

10
00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:54.281
Its three entries stay pending under its name, and their idle time keeps growing.

11
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:59.157
Asking for new entries won't return them, because they were already delivered.

12
00:00:59.157 --> 00:01:00.901
They aren't lost, only stuck.

13
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.373
So w3 runs XAUTOCLAIM with a threshold of 30 seconds.

14
00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:09.081
Every entry idle longer than that moves to w3.

15
00:01:09.081 --> 00:01:13.515
Its idle time resets, and its delivery count goes to 2.

16
00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:19.540
Pick the threshold above your slowest normal run, so a worker that's only slow keeps its entries.

17
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:24.210
w3 settles all three and acknowledges them, and the list is empty.

18
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:30.925
A crash between settling and acknowledging means a second delivery, so settling must be idempotent.

19
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:35.172
A consumer group remembers every delivery until it's acknowledged.

20
00:01:35.172 --> 00:01:40.128
When a worker dies, another claims its entries once they've sat idle long enough.
